  "conversation_weighting_strategy": "Each retained snapshot in conversation i gets base weight 1/n_i, so the conversation's base weights sum to 1. Let M_k be the sum of base weights on label k. class_factor_k = (M_0 + M_1) / (2 * M_k), which makes the total weight on YES equal the total weight on NO. unnormalized = base * class_factor[label]. final = unnormalized / mean(unnormalized), so the mean sample weight is 1 and the default L2 penalty stays on the usual scale. The global rescale does not change conversation ratios or the equal class totals. class_weight is left unset, because sklearn's balanced mode uses row counts and would undo the conversation weights. A mixed conversation's total moves with its YES/NO mix, because pre-onset NO snapshots are not given the fraud class factor.",
